        "cve": "CVE-2026-13221",
        "image": "php-8.3-8.4",
        "package": [
          "libperl5.36",
          "perl",
          "perl-base",
          "perl-modules-5.36"
        ],
        "classification": "false-positive-disputed-range",
        "evidence": "Debian's own notes say the flaw was 'Introduced with ... (v5.37.10)'; bookworm ships perl 5.36.0-7+deb12u3, which PREDATES that commit. NVD's 'versions up to (including) 5.43.9' range ignores the introduction point. Empirical probe on the installed build: a 70,000-branch fixed-string alternation compiled to a trie matched correctly at branches 1/100/65534/65535/65536/65537/69999/70000 with no false positives \u2014 the entire symptom of this CVE is absent."
      }
    },
